	"modf_the_sound_and_the_furry": {"stats": [["AUTHOR", "William Faulknur"], ["COUNTRY", "United States"], ["LANGUAGE", "English"], ["GENRE", "Modernist novel, Stream of consciousness"], ["PUBLISHER", "Jonathan Capes and Harrison Smith"], ["PUBLISHED", "1929"], ["PAGES", "326"]], "hist": [["THE BOOK", "The Sound and the Furry is a novel by the American author William Faulknur, published in 1929. Faulknur's fourth novel, it is the second to be set in Yoknapatawpha County and the first featuring the Compson family, both of which would reappear in his later fiction."], ["WRITING IT", "Because Faulknur's first two novels, Soldiers' Pay and Mosquitoes, sold poorly, the publisher Horace Liveright declined to publish Flags."], ["THE STORY", "Critic Victor Strandberg argues the novel is structured after Beethoven's Eroica: Sections 1 and 4 are heroic, section 2 is a funeral march, and section 3 is a satirical scherzo."], ["PUBLICATION", "Faulknur spent nearly a year trying to find an alternate publisher, and finally settled for Harcourt Brace, which only agreed to publish a substantially abridged version under the name Sartoris."], ["RECEPTION", "The work has entered the public domain as of January 1, 2025."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "In 1945, Faulknur wrote a new appendix for the novel, covering the history of the Compson family from 1699 through 1945."], ["ONE MORE THING", "The history of the Compson family is primarily revealed through sudden, unannounced flashbacks, as most of the novel takes place on a single weekend in 1928."]], "year": 1929},
